============================================================
TOPIC 1: FILE & DIRECTORY MANAGEMENT
============================================================

WINDOWS REFERENCE                  | LINUX COMMAND
------------------------------------------------------------
Open / go to a folder              | cd /var/log
Go one folder back                 | cd ..
Go to root directory               | cd /
Go to home directory               | cd ~
See files and folders              | ls
See detailed files                 | ls -l
See hidden files                   | ls -la
Create a folder                    | mkdir test
Create a new file                  | touch file.txt
Copy a file                        | cp file1.txt file2.txt
Move a file                        | mv file.txt /tmp/
Rename a file                      | mv old.txt new.txt
Delete a file                      | rm file.txt
Delete a folder                    | rm -r folder


============================================================
TOPIC 2: FILE VIEWING / EDITING
============================================================

WINDOWS REFERENCE                  | LINUX COMMAND
------------------------------------------------------------
Open / view a file                 | cat file.txt
View large file                    | less file.txt
View first 10 lines                | head file.txt
View last 10 lines                 | tail file.txt
Watch file continuously            | tail -f app.log
Edit a file                        | nano file.txt
Edit a file                        | vi file.txt
Search inside a file               | grep "error" file.txt
Search recursively                 | grep -r "error" /var/log


